\subsection{Binary Search Trees}

\begin{note}
A \emph{tree} is like a linked list, but has two recursive attributes instead of one.
A \emph{binary search tree} (BST) satisfies the invariant that:
every node in the left branch is less than or equal to val,
and every node in the right branch is greater than or equal to val.
This property lets us \emph{prune} branches of the tree when doing searches,
and makes searching much faster.
\end{note}
